---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Siren: AI Communications & MCP Tooling — Kiran S Baliga" }}>
	<article class="pt-6 pb-16 sm:pt-8 sm:pb-20">
		<a
			class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 mb-8 dark:text-neutral-400"
			href="/#work"
		>
			&larr; Back to selected work
		</a>

		{/* Article Header */}
		<header class="mb-10">
			<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
				Siren &middot; Engineering case study
			</span>

			<h1 class="font-sans text-[34px] leading-[1.3] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-6">
				Communication rails and MCP tooling for autonomous AI agents.
			</h1>

			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 max-w-2xl">
				At Siren, I engineered the developer infrastructure enabling AI agents to communicate: shared tool schemas, TypeScript and Python agent toolkits, and a standalone Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
			</p>

			{/* Role & Context Box */}
			<div class="border-y border-[#deded8] my-8 py-5 dark:border-neutral-800">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-3">
					<div>
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
							Associate Software Engineer
						</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
							KeyValue Software Systems &middot; Client engagement: Siren
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="sm:text-right">
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 tabular-nums">
							Sep 2023&ndash;Feb 2026
						</span>
						<a
							class="font-sans text-sm text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
							href="https://trysiren.com"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							trysiren.com &nearr;
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
					Model Context Protocol (MCP) &middot; TypeScript &middot; Python &middot; OpenAI Functions &middot; LangChain &middot; CrewAI
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		{/* Context */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				The context
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Siren provides omni-channel messaging and notification infrastructure. As autonomous agent workflows (OpenAI Function Calling, LangChain, CrewAI) began executing user-facing tasks, agents needed safe, deterministic ways to trigger notifications, verify recipients, and inspect delivery status without manual API integration.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				The core architectural goal was to turn imperative REST API endpoints into clean, agent-readable semantic tool schemas with strict parameter boundaries and deterministic execution safeguards.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Zero-Install MCP Server */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				Zero-install Model Context Protocol (MCP) server
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				I built and distributed <code class="font-mono text-sm bg-[#f8f7f4] dark:bg-neutral-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@trysiren/mcp</code>, a standalone server implementing Anthropic’s Model Context Protocol. Supporting both stdio and Server-Sent Events (SSE) transports, it allowed AI coding assistants (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Antigravity) to send notifications directly from developer environments.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				This eliminated ~75% of developer setup overhead: rather than installing libraries, importing HTTP clients, and managing secret rotation in application code, developers execute the server with zero installation via <code class="font-mono text-sm bg-[#f8f7f4] dark:bg-neutral-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">npx @trysiren/mcp</code>.
			</p>

			<div class="border-l-2 border-[#262625] dark:border-[#f5f4f1] pl-5 py-2 my-6">
				<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
					Making existing products AI-native doesn’t require rebuilding the backend. It requires building an intuitive, deterministic discovery and execution layer for models.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Dual-Stack SDKs & Idempotency */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				Dual-stack agent toolkits with idempotency guards
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				For programmatic multi-agent swarms, I authored and published <code class="font-mono text-sm bg-[#f8f7f4] dark:bg-neutral-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@trysiren/agent-toolkit</code> on npm and <code class="font-mono text-sm bg-[#f8f7f4] dark:bg-neutral-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">siren-agent-toolkit</code> on PyPI. Both feature automatic conversion adapters for LangChain Tools and CrewAI Actions.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Because LLM tool-calling can trigger stochastic retry loops, we embedded deterministic idempotency key derivation directly into the toolkits. Multiple identical intents from an agent resolve to the same underlying dispatch, preventing accidental notification spam.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* What Changed / Metrics */}
		<section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
				What changed
			</h2>

			<div class="space-y-5">
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						~75%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Reduction in developer setup effort with zero-install MCP vs. manual SDK integration.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						100+
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Peak registry downloads across npm and PyPI ecosystem distributions.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						&lt;1ms
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Serialization overhead across schema parsing and parameter validation pipelines.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Next Case Study */}
		<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-8 dark:border-neutral-800">
			<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2">
				<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">Next case study</span>
				<a
					class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
					href="/work/ultrahuman/"
				>
					Ultrahuman &mdash; clinical LLM pipelines &rarr;
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 mt-4">
				Building agent tooling or Model Context Protocol integrations? <a class="underline hover:text-accent" href="mailto:kiransbaliga@gmail.com">Let’s talk about it.</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
